    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1069">

                <pb facs="1098" n="978" sameAs="frus:frus1905/pg978"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        Minister Bowen.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1905-02-24"><hi rendition="#italic">February 24,
                        1905</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Referring to your dispatch of the 20th, the Department is of the opinion that
                    unless able to confirm them you should deny such defamatory reports concerning
                    superior officer, instead of seeming to give them weight by cabling. Your use of
                    the word “facts” seems unwarranted by any evidence before the Department.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hay</hi>.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
